  "sourceChanges": [
    {
      "file": "proj/src/pixelWings.c",
      "originalSha256": "ff33f66c3a43b53f3946b51eb509583590c704074bf5ccc9694d2ac10f885224",
      "patchedSha256": "bbc3205df08b519d1bef19327ed2c6b80006964853220c05b3230ab6fac9310c",
      "reason": "Malformed fscanf formats parsed20 rows from the pinned10-record score file, writing beyond scores[11] and overwriting currentDragon, so the player and its shots were invisible. Read complete bounded lines, validate the original count-name-score-date record, cap displayed scores at10 and close missing/malformed files safely. Actual owning parser RED corrupts player state with pinned original file; GREEN preserves dragon and adjacent state, original names/scores/date digits,12-character maximum,10-row limit and invalid/missing-file handling. Original score data and all artwork unchanged."
    },
    {
      "file": "proj/src/bitmap.c",
      "originalSha256": "37aa4cb30060446f84af9b295f4e21e3e4b152fe4c56e72e538da73915dec970",
      "patchedSha256": "55898a253cc1d4acd6b86e34b10ab3460d56779bbef5eb8fb072bcd06a7dd15a",
      "reason": "getPath passed its filename as sprintf format and copied through a fixed256-byte stack buffer. Actual percent-bearing path RED is changed by format expansion; original strict NDK -Wformat -Werror=format-security also fails. Allocate strlen+1 and copy literal bytes, preserving percent characters and complete longer paths. Actual owning helper GREEN on percent and599-character paths; all11ARM64units compile with actual FORTIFY/format-security flags."
    }
  ],
